WEBVTT

NOTE Edited transcription of a historical recording. Unclear speech is marked; use current specifications for ordering.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Welcome to the GOLA Channel Training Session for
Eclipse Frameless Cabinets.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.400
In this presentation, we'll cover how to
effectively design with GOLA channels and how to
integrate

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.400
them into base, tall, wall, and vanity cabinets.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:22.100
Here's an example of the GOLA channels in a
real-world kitchen.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.400
What is GOLA?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.000
The GOLA channel system offers a sleek, handle-
less design, perfect for achieving a minimalist

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.700
European aesthetic.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.400
The channels are long metal strips

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.200
that are attached to the fronts of cabinets

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.600
that create a recessed area that allows a user

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.100
to place their hands behind a drawer to open
them.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.800
The channels themselves are fixed on the
cabinets

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.700
and do not move when doors and drawers are
opened.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.400
This system eliminates the need for protruding
handles.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.800
And best of all, there's no drilling required

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.600
on the cabinet doors or drawers.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.800
That means a cleaner, more minimal look

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.600
and easier maintenance over time.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.900
For wall cabinets, the GOLA system is all about
subtlety.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.800
Unlike how the channel is visible on base
cabinets and tall cabinets,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.100
GOLA wall cabinets are designed without an
exposed channel.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.100
The eclipse cabinetry offers several options for
GOLA wall cabinets.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.600
The most simple and affordable option is to add
a recessed bottom shelf

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.400
RBS modification to a standard eclipse wall
cabinet.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.000
This option requires no hardware at all.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:32.000
The recessed bottom shelf creates an inch and a
half high space behind each door, allowing hand
access to open the door,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
but also creating that clean, invisible look.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
For a higher-tech alternative, Eclipse also
offers a GOLA LED continuous pull option.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:50.000
This involves a groove in the bottom shelf for
the GWL-CPA LED strip.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.800
However, please note that this pull is installed
in the field and must be ordered separately.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.400
Also keep in mind that the LED continuous pulls
are only available in the aluminum finish.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.700
Although they will be hidden behind any closed
doors, they will be visible every time the

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.100
door is opened.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.700
Your wall cabinet codes must also include FWC as
a prefix when ordering so that the

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:19.500
cabinets are prepped at the factory with the
groove to accept the LED strip.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:25.900
For those who prefer a push-to-open experience,
touch latches or tip-on hardware can be used.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:32.600
This is an alternative way to achieve a
handleless design without visible hardware or
channels.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:37.400
GOLA is most often used in base cabinets, and
that's where you'll find the most options.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.500
The Eclipse factory prepares all GOLA base
cabinets to accept two styles of horizontal

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.300
GOLA channel rails.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.300
The L channel is located at the top of the base
cabinet, just under the countertop.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.800
The C channel is placed between doors and
drawers.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.400
The channels come in 13 foot long pieces that
must be ordered separately.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.700
The channels are to be field installed across
several cabinets and they can be cut to length

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.600
to end where the channel terminates in the
design.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.200
For example, at the end of a run of base
cabinets where cabinets meet a wall or where a
door

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.400
meets a door in the neighboring cabinet.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:18.600
Also to know, all GOLA base cabinets use L
channel, but not all will use C channel
depending

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.000
on the configuration of doors and drawers in the
cabinet.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Some tall and vanity cabinets can also
incorporate the horizontal L and C channels,
mirroring

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:34.300
the base cabinet configurations.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:39.700
GOLA channels are available in six metallic
finishes, white lacquer, anodized aluminum,

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:46.500
stainless steel, slate, matte black, and gold
anodized.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.500
L channels and C channels each have their own
parts and accessories including corner

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.700
transition pieces and end caps.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:04:02.100
Refer to the Eclipse book pages R40 through R46
for L channels and R43 through R45 for

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:09.200
C channels to ensure that you're using the right
components in your design.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.000
Some utility tall cabinets are designed to use
vertical channels rather than horizontal

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.000
channels.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.600
cabinets vertical channels are integrated behind
the door on the side

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.700
opposite the hinge. These vertical rails can
connect between cabinets or between

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.300
a cabinet and an end panel. Please note that the
vertical channel will create

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:37.200
large gaps between cabinets and it will decrease
your storage space. Just like

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.400
standard eclipse cabinets, GOLA cabinets offer
finished ends at no additional

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:47.600
charge. However, GOLA channels need end caps to
finish them properly. Use open end caps for

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.900
exposed sides and closed end caps next to
appliances or when butting up against other
cabinets.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:01.600
Instead of using those end caps, you can also
opt for flush finished end panels. These panels

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:07.200
extend beyond the cabinet box, aligning flush
with the door or drawer face for a seamless
appearance.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:14.700
Here is an example of that in a 2020 design.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:20.200
Decorative end panels are also available in
multiple widths and must be specified by side.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:25.500
These match the cabinets configuration, whether
it's a single panel for a full height door

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.100
or a double panel for a door drawer combination.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:34.700
Remember these ship loose and require field
attachment.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.600
Side corner caps are used when channel wraps
around a corner, such as on an island.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.400
They help join the front and side channels
smoothly.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.500
Take inspiration from these real-world examples.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.900
Notice how different end panel options and
lighting features enhance the aesthetics of

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:59.300
each design, including floating effects and
seamless cabinetry.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:04.900
To design with GOLA in 2020, be sure to download
the separate GOLA Eclipse catalog from the

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.200
Portal or Dealer Resource website.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:13.800
While designing in 2020, don't forget to add all
channels, end caps, LED pulls, and accessories

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.800
to your item list.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:19.100
They are not automatically included with your
cabinets.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:24.700
Note that they may show under the Accessories
Extra Cost tab rather than your main item list,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:31.400
they will be listed on your WW Wood Products
Order Report when you place your order.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:35.300
Thank you for joining us for this GOLA Channel
Training.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:40.500
For questions, refer to the Eclipse catalog or
contact your sales rep for assistance.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:40.810
We're excited to see what you design using
Eclipse Cabinetry's GOLA system.
